        <item>
            <title>0.19.7</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:51:02 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1907</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.19.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.19.7</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Meeting action points reach Focus.</b> When you say in a meeting that
      you will do something, it now becomes a task — it could get lost when
      other messages arrived during the call. Meetings from the last week are
      checked once more when Jarvis opens.</li>
  <li><b>Tasks remember the meeting.</b> If a task Jarvis already found in
      Slack was also discussed in a meeting, the meeting now shows up under
      where the task came from.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
